            <h2>User Guide Overview</h2>

            <div class="main-content">
                
<p class="rvps2"><span class="rvts20">Naviate Cloud Manager </span><span class="rvts6">allows BIM 360® Administrators to quickly and easily perform many time-consuming and repetitive tasks:</span></p>
<ul style="text-indent: 0px; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 0 48px; list-style-position: outside; list-style-type: disc;">
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="AddNaviateCloudManagertoBIM360Hu.html">Add Naviate Cloud Manager to BIM360 Hubs</a><span class="rvts21">.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Connect to BIM 360® using the standard </span><a class="rvts43" href="AutodeskRConnection.html">Autodesk® Login</a><span class="rvts21"> or a pre-defined </span><a class="rvts43" href="CustomConnections.html">Custom Connection</a><span class="rvts21">.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Define multiple BIM 360® </span><a class="rvts43" href="Add.html">Custom Connections</a><span class="rvts21">, based on authorized access to an </span><a class="rvts22" href="AutodeskPlatformServicesAppDefin.html">Autodesk® App</a><span class="rvts21"> and </span><a class="rvts22" href="CustomIntegrationDefinition-Auto.html">Custom Integration</a><span class="rvts21">.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Add new </span><a class="rvts22" href="CreateNewProjects.html">projects</a><span class="rvts21"> to Autodesk® BIM 360®.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Add and update </span><a class="rvts22" href="AddFilestoProjects.html">documents</a><span class="rvts21"> to new and existing projects from a user-designated local folder structure.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Add and update </span><span class="rvts22">members</span><span class="rvts21"> for new and existing projects.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="ExportDatatoMicrosoftExcel.html">Export</a><span class="rvts21"> project data to a Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.&nbsp;</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="ProjectDetailsDisplay.html">Display</a><span class="rvts21"> folders, documents, file sizes and versions for specified projects directly from BIM 360®.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="DownloadFilestoLocalDisk.html">Download</a><span class="rvts21"> and update BIM 360® files and folder structure to local folders for designated projects.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="LatestHasBeenPublished.html">Display</a><span class="rvts21"> whether a file is an Autodesk® Revit® Cloud Workshared model and if the latest version has been published.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="PublishLatest.html">Publish</a><span class="rvts21"> the latest version of an Autodesk® Revit® Cloud Workshared model directly from the </span><span class="rvts23">Naviate Cloud Manager</span><span class="rvts21"> project browser.</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><a class="rvts22" href="AddaJob.html">Define</a><span class="rvts21">, </span><a class="rvts22" href="AddJobasaScheduledTask.html">deploy</a><span class="rvts21">, </span><a class="rvts22" href="JobExecution.html">execute</a><span class="rvts21"> and </span><a class="rvts22" href="StatusDisplay.html">monitor</a><span class="rvts21"> tasks that run according to a user-specified schedule and provide completion </span><a class="rvts22" href="JobInformation.html">notification and logging</a><span class="rvts21">. (Requires </span><span class="rvts42">Professional</span><span class="rvts21"> </span><a class="rvts22" href="License.html">license</a><span class="rvts21">).</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Define different </span><a class="rvts22" href="JobType.html">job types</a><span class="rvts21"> to perform various automated tasks. These include uploading and downloading files, </span><a class="rvts22" href="ExportType.html">exporting Revit® models</a><span class="rvts21"> as </span><span class="rvts42">PDF</span><span class="rvts21">, </span><span class="rvts42">NWC</span><span class="rvts21"> and </span><span class="rvts42">DWG</span><span class="rvts21">, as well as publishing Revit® Cloud Workshared models. (Requires </span><span class="rvts42">Professional</span><span class="rvts21"> </span><a class="rvts22" href="License.html">license</a><span class="rvts21">).</span></li>
 <li class="rvps12 noindent"><span class="rvts21">Deploy </span><a class="rvts22" href="ScheduledExecution.html">scheduled</a><span class="rvts21"> tasks to </span><a class="rvts22" href="RemoteServerSetupandConfiguratio.html">external computers</a><span class="rvts21">, including manual </span><a class="rvts22" href="RunDeployedJob1.html">start</a><span class="rvts21">, </span><a class="rvts22" href="StopRunningJob.html">stop</a><span class="rvts21"> and </span><a class="rvts22" href="StatusDisplay.html">status display</a><span class="rvts21"> capability. (Requires </span><span class="rvts42">Professional</span><span class="rvts21"> </span><a class="rvts22" href="License.html">license</a><span class="rvts21">).</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="rvps12"><span class="rvts21"><br/></span></p>
<p class="rvps12"><span class="rvts21"></span><span class="rvts21"></span></p>

